                <pb facs="0327" n="262" sameAs="frus:frus1936v03/pg262"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">124.84/64: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in the United Kingdom</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Bingham</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary
                        of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >London</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1936-05-04T00:00:00+01:00">May 4,
                        1936—midnight</date>.<lb/>[Received May 4—6:05 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>246. For Murray from the Ambassador. My 245. Foreign Office offers to telegraph
                    British Legation to send another armed convoy to evacuate entire American
                    Legation. Shall I ask Foreign Office to do so?</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Bingham</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
